# Whole-line comments only: systemd's EnvironmentFile keeps everything after `=` as the
# value, an inline comment included, and the guest then fails with "builder error".
# With egress gateways (ADR-0027 decision 3): a gateway's sandbox address and the control
# relay's broker port, by address, since the segment has no resolver; the pool's bootstrap
# list of gateways is /etc/mediatore/gateways (MEDIATORE_GATEWAYS_FILE to read another).
MEDIATORE_URL=https://mediatore.sandbox.example:8443
SPIFFE_ENDPOINT_SOCKET=/run/spire/sockets/agent.sock
RUST_LOG=info
# The per-claim sandbox tmpfs (ADR-0021): the kernel's size syntax; 50% of RAM when unset.
# MEDIATORE_SANDBOX_SIZE=4g
# Registries reached over plain HTTP, comma-separated; pin their images by digest.
# MEDIATORE_PLAIN_HTTP_REGISTRIES=registry.internal:5000
# A PEM of CA certificates trusted beside the Mozilla roots for the pull: the mirror on the
# segment on your PKI (ADR-0029); its address goes in /etc/mediatore/registries too.
# MEDIATORE_REGISTRY_CA=/etc/mediatore/registry-ca.pem
# The SPIRE bundle, fetched at every boot through a gateway's bundle leg (ADR-0037;
# image/spire-bundle-fetch). The hostname is the bundle endpoint's, as its certificate names
# it (the pin); the gateway is a sandbox address, the port the relay's RELAY_BUNDLE_PORT; the
# CA is a PEM of the roots that certificate chains to, the system store when unset. Leave
# SPIRE_BUNDLE_HOST out when the layer carries the bundle as a file.
# SPIRE_BUNDLE_HOST=spire.sandbox.example
# SPIRE_BUNDLE_PORT=3131
# SPIRE_BUNDLE_GATEWAY=198.51.100.1
# SPIRE_BUNDLE_CA=/etc/mediatore/bundle-ca.pem
# Registries reached through a gateway's registry leg (ADR-0038), for a pool with no registry on the
# segment: the registry's own name and the relay's RELAY_REGISTRY_PORT, comma separated; the gateway is
# the one MEDIATORE_URL names. The pull is root's: the host table admits the leg to uid 0 alone.
# MEDIATORE_RELAY_REGISTRIES=registry.example.com=3132
# What the egress proxy trusts when it reaches a host a policy bundle lists (direct egress), as the
# sandbox user, outside the jail. The first is a PEM of CA certificates trusted beside the Mozilla
# roots, for hosts on the operator's private PKI (the RBC bundle the image already carries is
# /etc/ssl/certs/rbc-ca-bundle.crt); without it only publicly trusted hosts verify. The second is the
# lowest TLS version offered: 1.3 (the default), or 1.2 for a host with no TLS 1.3 (an older GitHub
# Enterprise Server), which still offers 1.3 first. Neither reaches the broker, the identity provider,
# the registry pull or the sandbox leg, which stay TLS 1.3 only. The guest logs a warning at 1.2.
# MEDIATORE_EGRESS_CA=/etc/ssl/certs/rbc-ca-bundle.crt
# MEDIATORE_EGRESS_MIN_TLS=1.2
